    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test passing \u2014 the other two files in the acceptance package are support base classes, not test classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule in `ClinicServiceImpl.java`:\n\n- **`generateCustomerCode(Owner)`** now computes the base code (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`) as before, then passes it through a new de-duplication step.\n- **`deduplicateCustomerCode(String base)`** collects all existing owners' `customerCode` values. If the base code is unused, it's returned unchanged; otherwise it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n` \u2265 2 that isn't already taken (checking both the bare base and prior `-<n>` de-duplications).\n\nThis runs before membership-number generation, so the derived `membershipNumber` correctly picks up the de-duplicated code. Added the `java.util.stream.Collectors` import. The `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test \u2014 which asserts distinct owners always get distinct customerCodes \u2014 passes.",
