    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe extraction is clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- Splitting the base derivation (`generateCustomerCode`) from the collision-resolution (`deduplicateCustomerCode`) puts each concern in its own appropriately-sized, single-purpose private helper, matching the existing decomposition style in this class (`computeHouseholdId` / `householdKey` / `normalizeHouseholdKey`, `findHouseholdMembers`).\n- The new helper is placed right after its caller, consistent with the file's existing \"method then its helpers\" ordering.\n- `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()...` mirrors the established pattern in `findHouseholdMembers` (line 393), so a maintainer would find it natural; `Collectors.toSet()` is the correct idiom (no `Stream.toSet()` exists) and the import is the only incidental addition.\n- No logic is duplicated, and neither method becomes a catch-all \u2014 each stays tightly focused.\n- The Javadoc on both `generateCustomerCode` and `deduplicateCustomerCode` is updated to describe the new behavior, in keeping with the thorough doc style throughout the class.",
